  photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ffd6f7ee79716d146b73adb9d957ad8e, type: 3}
  title: "Ex-Cess \u2013 October '80 Programme, Die Neue Musik live!"
  description: "The October 1980 concert programme for Ex-Cess,\nKurf\xFCrstenstr.
    101, Berlin \u2014 a key West Berlin venue for\n'Die Neue Musik'. The line-up
    includes Fehlfarben (9.10),\nRadierer, ZK, K\xE4nguruhs im Ex-Cess, Toto-Lotto,
    \xD6stro 430,\nWhite Russia, and Hot Java Band."
  hasExtraInfo: 1
  extraInfoTitle: Ex-Cess and the Neue Deutsche Welle
  extraInfoContent: "Ex-Cess was one of West Berlin's important live venues\nduring
    the explosion of the Neue Deutsche Welle\naround 1980. This single monthly programme
    captures how\ndense and vital the scene was \u2014 featuring Fehlfarben,\nwhose
    1980 album 'Monarchie und Alltag' became\none of the most celebrated German-language
    records\never made, as well as \xD6stro 430, an all-female band from\nD\xFCsseldorf.
    The hand-drawn, cut-and-paste design of the\nposter is typical of the DIY aesthetic
    that defined the era's\nunderground graphics \u2014 the same spirit that shops\nlike
    Zensor embodied."
  extraInfoImage: {fileID: 0}
